<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    GH-9191: "Could not recover jumptable ... Too many branches" for a switch
    whose table index is bounded by a modulo (index % N) rather than a guard.
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/9191

    The dispatch computes  goto *(LOAD( (index % 5) * 8 + 0x401089 ))  with a
    5-entry address table at 0x401089:
        0x401034, 0x401042, 0x401050, 0x40105e, 0x40106c
    The basic jump-table model (jumptable.cc, JumpBasic) only bounds a table by
    an explicit CBRANCH guard or a direct INT_AND mask on the switch variable.
    A modulo bound (INT_REM/INT_SREM by a constant) on the LOAD-table index is
    not recognized, so the normalized variable defaults to the full width of the
    loaded value, the range exceeds maxtablesize, and recovery aborts.  The C
    then renders the dispatch as a computed call through a function pointer.

    Stage model: S2 "switch-model" sub-stage; the missing index bound starves
    jump-table recovery.  Fix surface = a default-off ArchOption
    (switchmodbound) that, when the normal model fails, walks the LOAD-table
    pointer chain for a modulo/and-mask bound and rebuilds the model so the
    table iterates the index over [0, N-1].

    Pass 1 (default, option off): assertion #1 proves the bug reproduces; the
    dispatch renders as a computed call to a function pointer (*(code *)...)().
    Pass 2 (option switchmodbound on): assertion #2 proves the table is bounded
    and the dispatch is recovered as a switch (no more "Too many branches").
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401014">

</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401014" name="jmpmod"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>lo fu jmpmod</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option switchmodbound on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH9191 #1: modulo-bounded switch renders as a computed call (bug reproduced)" min="1" max="1">\(\*\*\(code \*\*\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH9191 #2: switchmodbound on bounds the table and recovers the switch" min="1" max="1">switch\(</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
